00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.230
The history of loyalty--

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.790
again, DSW has been around
for quite some time.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.280
Originally, just
a brick and mortar

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.300
retailer, like most others.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.573
The loyalty program
actually started back then.

00:00:59.573 --> 00:01:01.990
In the late '90s, they actually
launched the first loyalty

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.010
program.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.420
It was called
Reward Your Styles.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.190
It was actually sourced and
supported outside of DSW.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:12.130
In 2004, we brought that
in-house, and then quickly

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.560
thereafter, in 2006, we
actually launched DSW Rewards.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.590
DSW Rewards, as you can
see from the timeline

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.870
there, while it
launched in 2006,

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.570
really didn't have much
change or impact to it

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:26.110
until we launched VIP
just this past September.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:29.170
We did implement over the course
of time there the experience

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.030
on our dot-com profile.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:34.510
We did implement that
in 2009, but when

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.290
we did that, that was
a customer's choice,

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.990
so we still had people that
could have a dot-com presence,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.110
but not be part of our loyalty,
and it added that confusion

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.540
to what they were
ultimately doing.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.510
You had people that
thought they were

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.060
in loyalty, people that didn't
think they were in loyalty.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.120
So in 2013, when we
rebranded and replatformed

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.660
our dot-com profile, we enrolled
everyone into the profile.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.645
When you go to DSW.com or if you
give us an email in your store,

00:01:55.645 --> 00:01:57.520
you're instantly into
our loyalty program now

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.455
to unify that across the board.

00:01:59.455 --> 00:02:01.330
I won't spend too much
time on the last part,

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.340
because that's the big meat
of how we got into VIP.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.840
The key thing to
talk about, though,

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.215
from this solution that they
had, even once we brought it

00:02:08.215 --> 00:02:09.850
in-house from the
original program,

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.270
was there was no dedicated
team to support it.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.850
If they needed data in, they'd
call somebody, whoever they

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:16.930
knew in our integrations team.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.010
If they needed
something modeled,

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.427
they'd have to go
with our BI team

00:02:19.427 --> 00:02:22.173
to change the internal
data model for them.

00:02:22.173 --> 00:02:23.590
So they just kind
of got in queue.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.645
They had no priority,
no emphasis on things,

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.770
so they would get creative.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.395
They would start doing
their own work arounds,

00:02:29.395 --> 00:02:30.895
doing things, and
coming to IT later

00:02:30.895 --> 00:02:32.110
and say, hey, you
have to do this,

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.580
because we've already
told our customers we're

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:34.955
doing this, which
would obviously

00:02:34.955 --> 00:02:37.300
create a lot of stir and
prioritization changes

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.860
on the IT side.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.050
We'd have data fixes that
were just done in a vacuum

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.730
that we then lived
through as we're

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.980
trying to implement and move
from an on-prem database

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.270
to a cloud database.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.448
All those fixes had to
become reality and new life

00:02:49.448 --> 00:02:49.990
in our world.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.360
What are the asks and needs
for the new loyalty program?

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.027
While this is DSW's
program, we honestly

00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:01.193
view this as our customer's
program, so we went out,

00:03:01.193 --> 00:03:01.860
and we surveyed.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.901
We asked the customers
what are they looking for.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:04.950
What do you want to do?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.140
What does DSW mean to you,
and what are you looking

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.345
for in our loyalty program?

00:03:10.345 --> 00:03:11.970
There was some key
things that came out

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.690
of that that really rope
up into these four points.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.540
Real-time everything-- we
lived in a batch-based world

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.470
where transactions came in
on a nightly sales screen.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.527
They were processed through,
and we would notify,

00:03:25.527 --> 00:03:28.110
hey, maybe you earned a reward
or maybe you earned a new tier,

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:31.182
but you don't get that reward
until seven days later.

00:03:31.182 --> 00:03:32.640
We've already lost
that engagement.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.400
We've lost that opportunity to
reconnect with that customer.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.525
We want to make sure we
can give them their points,

00:03:37.525 --> 00:03:39.240
give them their
tiers, communicate,

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.180
not just via email.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.408
We wanted to implement
and get more into SMS

00:03:42.408 --> 00:03:43.950
and app push
notifications, make sure

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.770
that customer recognizes that
you've transacted with us,

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.630
re-engage with us,
move this forward, keep

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.700
DSW in the front of their mind.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.630
Flexibility-- the
customers wanted more ways

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.180
to interact with us.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.520
We were a points-based
based on sales transactions.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.340
We wanted to be able
to give us your data,

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.737
give us the interaction,
give this point in a store,

00:04:02.737 --> 00:04:04.320
donate shoes, other
things they wanted

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.080
to do outside of just a
sales-based interactive

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.280
program.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.860
From a marketing standpoint,
they wanted the flexibility

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.320
to be able to move quickly.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.820
In their old world, they would
take up to two to three weeks

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.480
to set up a new promotion,
and it was XML based.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.170
You had to wait on
batches overnight,

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.420
where now we can react
in two to three hours.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.880
We can have a new promotion
set up and moving for them.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.780
A simplified program--
before points were 10 points

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.110
for $1.00, or 20, or 25, or
30, based on where you were

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.240
at, what promotions run,
so people would walk out

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.573
of the store not knowing did
I even get the right amount

00:04:35.573 --> 00:04:37.770
of points, what happened,
call the call center,

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:40.170
extra touch points, and
just confusion to what they

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.360
ultimately were trying to do.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.550
Then, ultimately, as we
looked at all those points,

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.050
we needed more data to
know about our customers.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.280
We want to make it more
personalized, more engaging,

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.010
and more opportunities to make
that experience their very own.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:56.610
That came in on the back
end along with IT's need

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.800
to align to marketing's needs.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.728
As I mentioned previously, there
wasn't a team to support that.

00:05:01.728 --> 00:05:03.270
Cam and I help make
up that team now,

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:04.800
we'll get into a
little bit more later,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.090
but we recognize that as a need.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.260
If we're really going
to jump into this

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.420
and deliver what the
business really needs,

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:10.920
we need to then,
in turn, give them

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.170
a team that they can come
to, and actually drive them

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.295
in line with their visions.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.810
With that, I'll
turn it over to Cam,

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.518
and he'll talk us
through our new loyalty

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:21.115
and how we got there.

